  "notes": "West's spade lead goes to East's ♠A. East continues spades and West wins. West will clear the spade suit. South has to make 2 discards from the dummy. What should they be?\n\nThe general concept of pitching low cards to keep high cards is a good one. On this deal, however, dummy has a very important low card that must be kept. The ♥2 has no value on this deal and can be discarded. The ♦2 is too big a little card to throw away.\n\nIf the ♦2 is discarded from dummy and clubs are 4-0, South will be able to cash just 7 tricks without surrendering the lead. The defense will be in a position to cash enough spade tricks to defeat the contract.\n\nIt should not be too difficult to part with a club from dummy's fine suit. South does not need 7 club tricks, just 3. Those tricks along with a spade trick, the ♥A, and 4 diamond tricks are enough to make 3NT.\n\nWith dummy retaining the ♦2 the suit can be played for 4 tricks (dummy's ♦A and ♦K must be cashed first). Notice also that South could have succeeded by discarding the ♦A and ♦K from dummy on the spades. However, he can't afford to part with the precious ♦2.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West's spade lead goes to East's ♠A. East continues spades and West wins. West will clear the spade suit. South has to make 2 discards from the dummy. What should they be?",
    "The general concept of pitching low cards to keep high cards is a good one. On this deal, however, dummy has a very important low card that must be kept. The ♥2 has no value on this deal and can be discarded. The ♦2 is too big a little card to throw away.",
    "If the ♦2 is discarded from dummy and clubs are 4-0, South will be able to cash just 7 tricks without surrendering the lead. The defense will be in a position to cash enough spade tricks to defeat the contract.",
    "It should not be too difficult to part with a club from dummy's fine suit. South does not need 7 club tricks, just 3. Those tricks along with a spade trick, the ♥A, and 4 diamond tricks are enough to make 3NT.",
    "With dummy retaining the ♦2 the suit can be played for 4 tricks (dummy's ♦A and ♦K must be cashed first). Notice also that South could have succeeded by discarding the ♦A and ♦K from dummy on the spades. However, he can't afford to part with the precious ♦2."
